Subject: [PATCH 2/7] Fix Schmitt threshold catch-22: scale-free ON(F) makes
 the bottom conquerable (H-A confirmed)

Diagnosis (exp_hypotheses.py): absolute ON=40 vs output cap w<=F//4 gave
accumulation asymptote 20w < ON for F<16 -- susceptibility windows could
never open from the bottom; all F0=10 duels deadlocked at (1,1), RL lost 0/10.

Hypothesis tests (exp_fix.py): ON x DECAY grid cannot fix an absolute
threshold; exchange-sign isolation shows bottom losses run through upkeep,
not the transfer law (H-C rejected as root cause); rest-curve is a secondary
factor (H-B). Scale-free hysteresis ON(F)=max(ON_MIN, ON_FRAC*F), OFF=0.4*ON(F),
plus MIN_OUTPUT=2 floor on committed work removes the catch-22 without new
state variables (verified first in isolated model copies sim_treat*.py).

Results: PRESSER opens windows and wins from F0=10 (was permanent draw);
mixed equilibrium preserved (TIMING still answers PRESSER, mirror pairs
symmetric); RL batch now wins 9/10 then 10/10 -- victory is again a property
of strategy. See FIX_HYPOTHESIS.md.
